# The esbuild invocation that produces core.bundle.js — the ONE copy of it.
#
# Both `make core-bundle` and TestVendoredBundleIsFresh read this file, so the
# rebuild and the freshness gate cannot drift apart: a flag changed here changes
# what is vendored AND what the gate expects, in the same commit.
#
# Everything except --outfile lives here (the target writes the vendored path,
# the gate writes a temp file). Paths are relative to the frontend checkout —
# both callers run esbuild with that as the working directory, which is what
# keeps the module-path comments esbuild emits identical between them.
#
# Blank lines and #-comments are stripped; every other line is one argument.
# See README.md in this directory for WHY each flag is what it is.

src/shared/core/index.ts

--bundle
--format=iife
--global-name=TypeMoreCore
--target=es2017
--platform=browser
--legal-comments=none
